{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Qasim, Son of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)",
  "data": "At the grave of Qasim, son of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), in Jannat al-Mu'alla, recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا سَيِّدَنَا يَا قَاسِمُ بْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAYYIDANAA YAA QAASIMUBNA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O our master, O Qasim, son of the Messenger of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ نَبِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAABNA NABIYYILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O son of the Prophet of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ حَبِيْبِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAABNA HABEEBILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O son of the beloved of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ الْمُصْطَفٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAABNAL MUSTAFAA\nPeace be upon you, O son of the Chosen One.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰى مَنْ حَوْلَكَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA A'LAA MAN HAWLAKA MINAL MU'MINEENA WAL MU'MINAAT\nPeace be upon you and upon the believing men and women around you.\nرَضِيَ اللّٰهُ تَعَالٰى عَنْكُمْ وَاَرْضَاكُمْ اَحْسَنَ الرِّضَا\nRADIYALLAAHU TA'AALAA A'NKUM WA ARDAAKUM AHSANAR RIDAA\nMay Allah, the Exalted, be pleased with you and make you pleased with the best of pleasure,\nوَجَعَلَ الْجَنَّةَ مَنْزِلَكُمْ وَمَسْكَنَكُمْ وَمَاْوَاكُمْ\nWA JA'ALAL JANNATA MANZILAKUM WA MASKANAKUM WA MA'WAAKUM\nand make Paradise your home, your dwelling and your refuge.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAYKUM WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.",
  "merits": "Qasim was the son of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and Lady Khadijah (s.a.), born in Makkah before the mission, and the Prophet was called Abu al-Qasim after him. He died as a small child and is buried in al-Hajun, now Jannat al-Mu'alla, near his mother.\n\nImam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that when Qasim died, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) came leaning on Zayd ibn Harithah, and passing Mount Abu Qubays he said: \"If what is in me were in you, O mountain, it would crush you.\" (Mustadrak al-Wasa'il 2:386)\n\nSayyid Muhammad Rida al-Golpayegani gives this ziyarat in his Manasik al-Hajj (p. 171)."
}
